            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="DIG01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Charles</forename>
                        <surname>Dignum</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1765">?
    <placeName> </placeName></birth>
                    <death when="1827-03-29"/>
                    <occupation>singer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>This may be Charles Dignum, the singer.  There are some links through Vauxhall, in the summers where Dignum was a regular performer, and some links to the theatre.  
      Godwin attended the first London performance of
      Haydn's <title>The Creation</title>, in which Dignum took part.  Dignum married in 1787, and his wife died in 1799, when there are no further instances of 'Dignums' (plural, hence incicating a couple).
      The main individual link seems to be through <persName key="FEL01">Ralph Fell</persName>.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">See <title>DNB</title></bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
